// Three secret placeholders chained through their shared delimiters: each
// candidate's terminator `__` is the next one's opening, and the last ends
// the run. The middle secret's body is then left behind as literal content
// of no match at all — the first candidate terminated on the middle's
// opening `__`, the overlap-aware prefix count treated the middle prefix as
// covered by that match, and the middle body leaked as ordinary text while
// the first and last lowered to engine lookups. The guard refused a
// terminator only when it opened a COMPLETE placeholder; here the middle
// candidate is itself chained — its terminator opens yet another prefix —
// so the guard let the first one through. Lowering refuses the text
// instead: a terminator may not open a chained placeholder, no candidate
// can end on another one's opening, and the orphaned prefixes fail the
// overlap-aware count. (The bodies below are well-formed so the leak is
// the only defect in play: with malformed bodies the third placeholder's
// own parse error masks the bypass.)
// expect: File content contains a malformed secret reference
// expect-pkl: File content contains a malformed secret reference
amends "modulepath:/ruxel/Workflow.pkl"
import "../inventory.pkl"

stages { new Stage { title = "t"; hosts = inventory.workers; steps {
  new File {
    path = "/etc/app/app.env"
    mode = "0600"
    content = "P=__ruxel_secret_8d41.f2:AB__ruxel_secret_8d41.f2:XA__ruxel_secret_8d41.f2:ZQ__\n"
  }
} } }
